Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:14:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] =?UTF-8?q?wacc:=20queryIn=20=E2=80=94=20where=20a=20n?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ame=20is=20declared,=20and=20its=20type,=20for=20an=20editor?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

queryIn(paths, sources, res, file, offset) answers what the token at an
offset is: its type, where it is declared, that declaration's line and its
doc comment, one fact a line.

The definition is found by reading (query.wac): the nearest declaration in
an enclosing scope — local, parameter, loop variable, match or pattern
binding, lambda parameter — then the file's top level, then its imports,
followed through export lists. A member a.b is looked up in the declaration
of a's type and its parents.

The type, and a's type, come from the checker: checkStmt now ends with a
probe (probe.wac) that, when C.probeTok is set, records the type of the
expression that token keys, with exactly the names in scope the statement
was checked with. Nested statements are probed first, so the innermost
answers. queryIn checks just the file's closure, as diagnoseGraphIn does
for each file, so a query costs about what checking that file does.

query.wac is written in the ladder's subset, as the rest of wacc is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
